    {
      "id": "43466d6b-87e7-4005-bcf0-894a63998376",
      "name": "Sticky Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        96,
        -448
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 480,
        "height": 912,
        "content": "## Instagram FAQ Automation Bot using RAG\n\n### How it works\n\n1. The workflow triggers either on a scheduled interval or when a new Instagram message or Google Drive file event occurs.\n2. Instagram messages are validated and processed by an AI agent to generate responses which are then sent back as DMs.\n3. New files created on Google Drive are filtered by MIME type, split into batches, downloaded, and stored in a Qdrant vector store.\n4. Sub-nodes within the AI Agent handle chat memory, vector storage, and interaction with a Google Gemini chat model.\n5. Several entry points allow embeddings generation, document loading, and text splitting for further processing or indexing.\n\n### Setup steps\n\n- [ ] Configure Instagram credentials and set up triggers for receiving messages and refreshing access tokens.\n- [ ] Set up Google Drive credentials and permissions for monitoring file creation and downloading files.\n- [ ] Configure access to the Qdrant vector store for storing and retrieving embeddings.\n- [ ] Set up Google Gemini API credentials for embedding generation and chat model interaction.\n- [ ] Adjust filters and conditions in the conditional nodes to match desired MIME types and chat validation criteria.\n\n### Customization\n\nUsers can customize the AI Agent by modifying the sub-nodes like chat memory size or the language model used. The triggers and conditions can also be tuned to fit specific Instagram accounts or Google Drive folders."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
